!Sample_taxid_ch1 = 9606
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = tissue: blood plasma
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = Sex: male
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = age: 48
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = disease state: early-onset CAD
!Sample_characteristics_ch1 = batch: S7504
!Sample_treatment_protocol_ch1 = No experimental treatment was applied; patients received standard clinical care, and fasting blood was drawn before or 24 h after heparin administration.
!Sample_molecule_ch1 = total RNA
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Peripheral venous blood was collected into EDTA tubes, centrifuged at 4 °C to separate plasma, and supernatant aliquots were stored at −80 °C. Total RNA enriched for miRNAs was isolated from plasma using Qiagen miRNeasy Serum/Plasma (CeGaT projects S7504, S8141) or miRNeasy Serum/Plasma Advanced kits (S10467) according to the manufacturer’s protocol.
!Sample_extract_protocol_ch1 = Small RNA libraries were prepared from plasma-derived RNA using commercial microRNA library preparation kits. For CeGaT projects S7504 and S8141, the NEXTFlex Small RNA-Seq v3 kit (Bioo Scientific) was used with the maximum possible RNA input per sample (up to approximately 10.5 µl). For CeGaT project S10467, libraries were prepared with the QIAseq miRNA Library Kit (Qiagen) using up to 5 µl RNA input. Library preparation followed the manufacturers’ protocols and included 3′ and 5′ adaptor ligation to small RNAs, reverse transcription, PCR amplification with indexed primers, and size selection to enrich fragments corresponding to adapter-ligated microRNAs. Final libraries were quantified, quality-controlled by fragment analysis and pooled equimolarly. Sequencing was performed on an Illumina NovaSeq 6000 platform with single-end reads (1 × 51 bp or 1 × 72 bp, depending on the sequencing run).
!Sample_description = Library name: KG30
!Sample_description = EDTA plasma sample from a participant with early-onset coronary artery disease; CeGaT ID S7504Nr21, external ID KG30.
!Sample_data_processing = Base calling and demultiplexing of raw sequencing data were performed with Illumina bcl2fastq (version 2.20) to generate per-sample FASTQ files according to the supplied index sequences.
!Sample_data_processing = Adapter sequences were removed with Skewer v0.2.2; no additional quality trimming was applied. Read quality was assessed using FastQC and summarized with MultiQC.
!Sample_data_processing = To remove remaining adapter sequence fragments and filter reads by length, miRDeep2 (version 2.0.1.3) was used. Only reads consistent with the expected miRNA length (18 nt) were retained for further analysis.
!Sample_data_processing = Reads were aligned to the human genome with Bowtie v1.0.0 within the miRDeep2 pipeline, using GRCh38.p13 and miRBase v22.1 mature and hairpin miRNA reference sequences for miRNA identification and quantification.
!Sample_data_processing = For each sample, miRNA-level read counts were extracted from the miRDeep2 output. Where multiple precursors corresponded to the same mature miRNA, median read counts were calculated to correct for redundancy. Low-abundance miRNAs were filtered (median count ≥10 in at least one group).
!Sample_data_processing = Assembly: Human reference genome GRCh38.p13 (Ensembl) with mature and hairpin miRNA annotations from miRBase release 22.1.
!Sample_data_processing = Supplementary files format and content: comma-separated file includes raw counts for each Sample
!Sample_platform_id = GPL24676
!Sample_contact_name = Evija,,Kanašniece
!Sample_contact_email = Evija.Kanasniece@rsu.lv
!Sample_contact_institute = Riga Stradins University
!Sample_contact_address = Dzirciema street 16
!Sample_contact_city = Riga
!Sample_contact_zip/postal_code = LV-1007
!Sample_contact_country = Latvia
!Sample_instrument_model = Illumina NovaSeq 6000
!Sample_library_selection = size fractionation
!Sample_library_source = transcriptomic
!Sample_library_strategy = miRNA-Seq
!Sample_relation = BioSample: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/biosample/SAMN53338578
!Sample_relation = SRA: https://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/sra?term=SRX31223135
!Sample_supplementary_file_1 = NONE
